---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const globalData = await getEntry("global", "site");
if (!globalData) throw new Error("Global site data not found");
const { site } = globalData.data;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How HealthShores collects, uses, shares and protects your personal and health information."
  updated="9 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    HealthShores ("<strong>HealthShores</strong>", "<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>us</strong>") is a medical
    tourism facilitator based in Bengaluru, India. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, share and
    protect your personal data when you visit www.healthshores.com (the "<strong>Website</strong>"), contact us,
    or use our services. We process personal data in accordance with India's Digital Personal Data Protection
    Act, 2023 and other applicable laws.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details:</strong> your name, email address and phone number.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiry details:</strong> the message you send us, which may include information about your
      health, medical condition or treatment needs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Information needed to arrange treatment</strong> (only if you choose to proceed): medical reports,
      test results, scans and photographs; passport and identity details; travel dates; and details of any
      companion travelling with you.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser and device type, and pages visited, collected by our
      hosting and security provider to deliver the Website and protect it from abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics and advertising data:</strong> we use Cloudflare Web Analytics (which does not use
      cookies) and Google tools loaded through Google Tag Manager, such as Google Analytics and Google Ads, which
      may set cookies to measure visits and the performance of our ads. See section 6.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your enquiry and provide a free consultation.</li>
    <li>To obtain treatment opinions and cost estimates from partner hospitals and doctors.</li>
    <li>
      To coordinate your treatment and travel, including hospital appointments, visa invitation letters,
      accommodation, airport transfers and translators.
    </li>
    <li>To stay in touch before, during and after your treatment, including follow-up care.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure and improve the Website.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use your health information for advertising.</p>

  <h2>3. Legal basis and consent</h2>
  <p>
    We process your personal data on the basis of your consent, which you give when you submit our contact form
    or share documents with us, and where necessary to provide the services you request or to meet legal
    requirements. Because health information is especially sensitive, we share it with hospitals or doctors only
    for the purpose of your enquiry or treatment.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can withdraw your consent at any time by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    Withdrawal does not affect processing that already took place, but we may no longer be able to assist with
    your treatment.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who we share your information with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Partner hospitals, doctors and clinics</strong> in India, so they can review your case, give
      opinions and cost estimates, and provide treatment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Travel and local service providers</strong> (for example hotels, transport and translators), limited
      to what they need to serve you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Government authorities</strong> where needed for your medical visa, or where required by law.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technology providers</strong> who process data on our behalf: Cloudflare (website hosting and
      security and privacy-friendly analytics), Resend (delivery of contact form emails), our email provider, and
      Google (analytics and advertising).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our patients live around the world and some of our technology providers operate outside India, so your data
    may be transferred to and stored in other countries. We only transfer data as permitted by applicable law and
    take reasonable steps to ensure it remains protected.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The Website uses a small number of cookies. Some are strictly necessary for security. Others are set by Google
    tools loaded through Google Tag Manager:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> measures how visitors use the Website so we can improve it.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Ads</strong> measures whether our ads lead to enquiries, and may be used to show our ads to
      people who have visited the Website. We never share the content of your enquiry or any health information
      with Google.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We also use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts visits without cookies and without tracking you across
    other websites.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and the Website will still work. You can manage how
    Google uses your data for ads at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>,
    and opt out of Google Analytics with the
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep your information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry information for as long as needed to respond and to follow up on your enquiry. If you become
    a patient, we keep your records for as long as needed to coordinate your treatment and follow-up care, and as
    required by law. When data is no longer needed, we delete it or make it anonymous.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How we protect your information</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data, including encrypted (HTTPS)
    connections and limiting access to people who need it. No method of transmission or storage is completely
    secure, so please avoid sending documents you don't need to share.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable law, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Get a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how we use it.</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct, complete or update your data.</li>
    <li>Ask us to erase your data when it is no longer needed.</li>
    <li>Withdraw your consent.</li>
    <li>Nominate another person to exercise your rights if you die or become incapacitated.</li>
    <li>Raise a grievance with us and, if unresolved, with the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details below.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries for patients under 18 must be made by a parent or legal guardian, who gives consent on the child's
    behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when it last
    changed.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact and grievances</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions, requests or complaints, contact our Grievance Officer:</p>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>HealthShores, Grievance Officer</strong><br />
    {site.address}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phone.replace(/\s/g, "")}`}>{site.phone}</a>
  </div>
  <p>We aim to respond to all requests within 30 days.</p>
</LegalLayout>
